# Cline-tuned Qwen2.5-Coder with bigger context for the bake-off.
#
# Why this exists
# ---------------
# Stock `qwen2.5-coder:7b` declares the `tools` capability but in practice
# emits raw JSON instead of the `<tool_call>...</tool_call>` wrapper that
# Ollama's parser needs. Result: every "tool call" lands in `content`,
# `tool_calls` stays `null`, and the Cline agent loop bails out after one
# iteration with no work done (confirmed via direct /api/chat probe).
# Known issue:
#   - continuedev/continue#6178 ("Tools stopped working and only respond with json")
#   - opencode#2728/#7030 (qwen2.5-coder tools "execute" but nothing happens)
#
# Cline community fix: use a tool-call-fine-tuned derivative. `hhao/qwen2.5-coder-tools:7b`
# is the most-used variant — same Qwen2.5-Coder weights, retrained to emit
# the wrapper reliably.
#
# Why 65536 num_ctx
# -----------------
# Cline's system prompt + workspace tool defs run ~30-40K tokens before the
# task even starts. The stock 4096 (or even 32K) silently truncates the tool
# section, which is another way tool calls quietly disappear.
# Source: cline/cline#241 — "The prompt of Cline is VERY LONG and 32768 is
# not enough to read in all the system prompt and your prompt."
#
# Lower temperature
# -----------------
# Local 7B models drift on long structured outputs at default temp (0.8).
# 0.2 keeps the tool-wrapper format stable across iterations.
#
# Build
# -----
#   ollama create cline-qwen:7b -f config/ollama/cline-qwen.Modelfile
#
# Use
# ---
# In .env:  OLLAMA_MODEL=cline-qwen:7b

FROM hhao/qwen2.5-coder-tools:7b

PARAMETER num_ctx 65536
PARAMETER temperature 0.2
PARAMETER top_p 0.9
